<article class="env-definition" id="0095">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0095">Definition <span data-tag="0095">6.26.1</span>.</a> Let $(f, f^\sharp ) : (X, \mathcal{O}_ X) \to (Y, \mathcal{O}_ Y)$ be a morphism of ringed spaces. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. We define the <em>pushforward</em> of $\mathcal{F}$ as the sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ Y$-modules which as a sheaf of abelian groups equals $f_*\mathcal{F}$ and with module structure given by the restriction via $f^\sharp : \mathcal{O}_ Y \to f_*\mathcal{O}_ X$ of the module structure given in Lemma <a href="/tag/008W" data-tag="008W">6.24.5</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ Y$-modules. We define the <em>pullback</em> $f^*\mathcal{G}$ to be the sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules defined by the formula 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  f^*\mathcal{G} = \mathcal{O}_ X \otimes _{f^{-1}\mathcal{O}_ Y} f^{-1}\mathcal{G}  \]
</div>
<p>
 where the ring map $f^{-1}\mathcal{O}_ Y \to \mathcal{O}_ X$ is the map corresponding to $f^\sharp $, and where the module structure is given by Lemma <a href="/tag/008X" data-tag="008X">6.24.6</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>